---

Why this file exists, and one decision still open.

All fourteen Solidity files in this repository already carry
`// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT` in their headers, and the source verified on
Blockscout against the deployment at 0x3744E93B9e796E05CB66311d897559B6F3860196
declares MIT publicly. A repository with no LICENSE file defaults to
all-rights-reserved, which would contradict a licence grant that has already been
published on a public chain. This file resolves that contradiction rather than
making a new choice.

The choice itself is still worth making deliberately before this repository goes
public. MIT permits anyone to fork Remit, including commercially, with no
obligation beyond attribution. That is the norm for infrastructure and it is a
reasonable position. Some protocols in this space instead ship under BUSL-1.1,
which reserves commercial use for a fixed term before converting to an open
licence, precisely to prevent an immediate competing deployment. Changing the
licence now is possible — the deployed bytecode does not encode it, only the
verified source metadata does — but it becomes considerably more awkward once
third parties have relied on MIT.

While this repository is private, the licence grants nobody anything and the
decision costs nothing to defer. Settle it before flipping to public.
